# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env — it is gitignored.
#
# Point this at a Neon branch you are allowed to break — never pilot or main:
#   UI-test  ep-little-violet  the UI rebuild, seeded with demo data  <- for UI work
#   dev      ep-red-shadow     backend/audit work
#   pilot    ep-curly-frost    served live, the tester's data
#   main     ep-round-sea      reserved for real books
#          (called "production" in the Neon console)
#
# Writing to pilot or main from a local command is a deliberate, one-off act:
# pass that URL explicitly on the command line rather than putting it here.
# The sidebar company name is the only way to tell them apart from inside the
# app, so check it before trusting anything:
#   "MTK Co Ltd — UI"    UI-test
#   "MTK Co Ltd — DEV"   dev
#   "MTK Co Ltd"         pilot   <- the tester's live data, stop
#   "My Company"         main
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-red-shadow-xxxxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require

# A local Postgres works too, if you would rather not touch a cloud branch:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://erp_dev:PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5433/myanmar_erp_dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- files ----
#
# Cloudflare R2, two buckets, split by who may read what is in them:
#
#   private  scanned bills, signed delivery notes, photographs of damage.
#            Evidence about a transaction. Served only through this app, and
#            the bucket must NOT be given a public URL or a custom domain.
#   public   product photographs. Fetched on every catalogue page, worth
#            nothing to a stranger, served straight from the edge.
#
# One API token covers both — Object Read & Write, scoped to these two
# buckets and nothing else. Account ID is in the R2 sidebar; the token's
# secret is shown once, at creation.
#
# Leave these unset and uploads are refused with a message saying so —
# nothing else in the app stops working.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET_PRIVATE=
R2_BUCKET_PUBLIC=
# The public bucket's read address: its r2.dev subdomain, or a custom domain
# if you connect one. No trailing slash. The private bucket has no equivalent
# and must not be given one.
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
